  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PADEO Learning Facilitator</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Embassy of the Netherlands in Maputo, Mozambique, aims to support a system approach towards leveraging local private sector development with focus on youth entrepreneurship and employment in the food and nutrition sector. The system that has been chosen to work for PADEO (Programmatic Approach Sustainable Economic Development) in Mozambique is the transition from subsistence farming to commercial farming with an emphasis on stimulating jobs for youth in this sector, from farmers and producers to the market, in the two focus areas of the Multi-annual country strategy (MACs 2023-2026): Cabo Delgado and the Beira Corridor.The Learning Facilitator supports the PADEO initiative by facilitating learning sessions, continuous data collection and guiding reflection processes to ensure improvement and adaptation of interventions. A local external learning facilitator who can guide the reflexive monitoring process will ensure that there is sufficient capacity to continuously learn throughout the process.    By building the bridge between lessons learned from the existing programs with the wider food and nutrition interventions in the system, the project facilitates the reflexive monitoring and learning process for PADEO in Mozambique. The continuous learning will ensure adaptability and the possibility to work in a complex change environment, such as the envisioned systems change needed to create job opportunities for youth in the agri-food sector.</narrative>
  </description>
